  "note": "Municipal elections, 15 May 1936. Only eleven names were put forward for fifteen seats, so there was no poll; the nominated candidates were returned unopposed and retiring members were declared deemed re-elected, leaving one Central Ward vacancy (Lisburn Standard, 8 May 1936, p. 5). Two nominations; retiring members Robert James Chambers and James Frazer were declared deemed re-elected. Returned unopposed."
